# PROPOSAL — THE KILL, CORRECTED (count-cut only, re-ruled 2026-10-25 on run-47's measurement)

Bring-for-ruling. NOTHING in this file is landed. Every hunk is old-text →
new-text against the tree as it stands (`attn-contract` HEAD ee1ca99b3 +
landed B + the landed, audited accumulator). Line numbers cite the current
file. This replaces `kill-hunk.diff` (r1, REJECTED AS PROPOSED — the
per_rung sweep never runs on the prefix-free path; kept on disk for the
record).

## The corrected ruling (restated)

Run-47's build.log shows every ktir_prefill window with exactly FOUR
bundles — prefix / body / body+'f' / suffix — and ZERO "ladder rung …
baked" lines: `chunk_ceiling.is_none()` for prefix-free emissions, so the
`:11686` gate never opens the sweep and there is no `rung_staged` content
to reclassify. The counted pair at each prefix-free rung is the PRIMARY
body (NONE-form, `:11431`) + the PRIMARY TWIN (`:11510`, minted by the
`:11497` arm — `card && chunk_ceiling.is_none()` is exactly the prefill
case; the `+f` dirs in the dump root are PRIMARY twins). The kill flips
the PRIMARY SPLIT to `counts_toward_total=false`; the TWIN stays in
`stage_fps`, counted — it is LIVE (chunk-0's RungFused). The kill is
LOAD-BEARING, not an optimization: without it the 256 rung's door reads
1 + 2×(~49k) + 45 ≈ 97-102k > 92,000 ⇒ the rung refuses ⇒ the ladder is
empty ⇒ the window guard fails the build; with it the door reads ≈49-51k
⇒ GREEN with headroom. The 512 rung still refuses at the body door
(:11438-11443) — the per-bundle wall fires inside `emit_bundle` at
render, pre-ticket, flag-ungated — so the ladder tops at 256 until
fusion. Body trips are NOT confirmed 48.2k (6,209 @ m=31 = 200/row,
96,429 @ m=512 = 188.3/row — the per-row rate falls with m); run-48's
census calibrates the 256 body.

The split stays emitted, submitted, staged, compiled, resolvable:
`body_fps.push(fp)` is UNTOUCHED (the ceiling rung's bodies and
RerollMeta's anchor keep the fp), manifest, rungs list, reach records,
and the selector's inputs are unchanged. The twin push `:11510` and its
Err catch `:11518-11524` are untouched. The per_rung classification
`:11821-11831` is untouched — r1's hunks 1-3 are withdrawn entire. No
wrapper change (its `filter(|t| t.counts_toward_total)` already drops the
flag); no serial-ladder door change.

## The discriminator (unchanged from r1, ruled correct)

The flip keys on the closure's own `active_cap` parameter:
`active_cap == superdsc::ActiveCap::NONE`. The closure signature is
`:11005`; `:13409` (the serial prefix-free ladder) is the ONLY call site
passing NONE; the tree's own keyings are `:12417-12424` (numeric gate)
and `:12443` (prefix-capable filter); `:12311-12322` is the tree's own
comment naming NONE the prefix-free marker. The prefix-capable ladder
passes FULL (`:13518`); decode passes `decode_ladder(cap)`/FULL.

